      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Compute the gradient of the function $f:{R}^{4}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x\n$$\n\n with respect to $x$ at $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)={b}^{T}x.\n$$\n\nThe gradient of a function $f(x)={b}^{T}x$ with respect to $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{x}f(x)=b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
